The library folder contains core functionality for managing digital library data including books, notes, and user content through IndexedDB storage. It provides shared TypeScript types and utilities for rendering library previews, serving as the foundation for all library-related operations in the application. Phase E (2026-08) added optional per-account cloud sync (librarySync.ts, against the C# backend's item-level library/my-writings/* endpoints) and tag-based grouping / line-char-limit stats to bring this client's editor to parity with the mobile client's. Organizations Phase 2 Step 5 (2026-08) added a second, deliberately separate content model alongside personal parchment/notes/books: org-content-types.ts/org-content.ts, for shared org-owned content fetched live (Bearer auth, no IndexedDB mirror — see org-content.ts's own purpose line for why) and rendered via components/OrganizationsPane.tsx.

Unsaved-changes rules (2026-10-31): unsavedChanges.ts decides whether the editor holds something a navigation would lose, for parchment, notes, book pages and organization items. A draft is compared with what is saved, so an edit typed back to the saved text is not dirty; a tag is compared trimmed (blank = no tag); an organization title and folder path are compared the way the save normalizes them (trimmed segments, max depth); an organization's spool counts only for notes. With nothing open nothing is dirty. One wording (discardMessage) for every confirmation. The mobile client keeps a hand-copied twin for organizations in dsl-client/features/organizations/unsaved-changes.ts: change both together.
